# The declared builtin inventory (EigenLua#21, #3): every global of the
# reference interpreter and every field of its library tables, one line each,
# as `<name> <D row>` (a Tier D program whose code, outside comment lines,
# names it: `lib.k`, or the string "k" for a library field it reaches by key;
# a base name not after '.' or ':') or `<name> uncovered: <reason>`.
# tools/grade.sh lists the names from the reference itself and exits 2 unless
# this list equals them both ways, every cited row is a manifest row, and
# every cited row names its builtin (plants builtin-missing, builtin-uncited).
